//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
//
// The CIL instruction set of ECMA-335 Partition III as an X-macro:
//
//   CIL_OPCODE(Enum, Text, Value, Operand, Pop, Push, Flow)
//
// One entry per opcode, 219 in all, in value order: the 218 opcodes of
// System.Reflection.Emit.OpCodes plus ECMA's 'no.' prefix (0xFE19).
//   Enum     the cli::Opcode enumerator (the System.Reflection.Emit field
//            name: '.' in the mnemonic becomes '_');
//   Text     the ILAsm mnemonic;
//   Value    0x00XX for a one-byte opcode, 0xFEXX for a two-byte opcode
//            (cli::TwoByteOpcodePrefix followed by XX);
//   Operand  the cli::OperandKind of the inline operand;
//   Pop, Push
//            cli::StackBehaviour names: what the instruction pops and pushes;
//   Flow     the cli::FlowControl name.
// Values and operand kinds follow ECMA-335 Partition III; Pop, Push and Flow
// are the StackBehaviour and FlowControl values of
// System.Reflection.Emit.OpCodes. The table was checked against
// System.Reflection.Emit, System.Reflection.Metadata's ILOpCode and the
// bytes that both ilasms assemble (llvm/docs/MSIL/recon/p2/metadata-writer.md,
// 3.7).
//
// The user defines CIL_OPCODE before including this file; the file #undef's
// it at the end.
//
//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//

#ifndef CIL_OPCODE
#error "define CIL_OPCODE before including CILOpcodes.def"
#endif

CIL_OPCODE(Nop, "nop", 0x0000, InlineNone, Pop0, Push0, Next)
